# Spider Swing — ignore rules
#
# Principle: Godot's text-native project files ARE the source of truth and are
# committed (.gd, .tscn, .tres, project.godot, export_presets.cfg). Everything
# the engine, the Android toolchain, or a local editor regenerates is ignored.
#
# No Git LFS: this repository has no large binary assets yet, and introducing
# LFS before real ones exist adds a clone-time dependency for nothing. Revisit
# when actual production art lands (see docs/technical/repository-layout.md).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Godot engine
# Regenerated import cache, UID cache, shader cache, and editor-local state.
.godot/
.import/
*.translation

# Godot writes per-machine editor state here; never share it.
export_presets.cfg.bak
.godot-version.bak

# --------------------------------------------------------- editor-local state
# Per-developer editor/IDE state that must not travel between machines.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ------------------------------------------- Android generated build state
# `gradle_build/use_gradle_build` produces this tree; it is machine-local.
/android/
!/android/README.md
/android/build/
/android/.gradle/
.gradle/
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
*.aar
*.idsig

# ------------------------- local export credentials and signing material
# NEVER commit production signing material. Production signing is
# owner-controlled and lives outside the tree (ADR 0003). The one explicit
# exception below is the public, conventional Android DEBUG key used only so
# consecutive laboratory APKs can update in place and preserve device saves.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pepk
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
export_credentials.cfg
!.github/android/debug.keystore

# Play release signing (ADR 0005). The upload key lives in repository secrets
# and is materialised only inside a CI runner's temp directory; none of these
# may ever appear in the tree. Base64 is called out explicitly because a
# keystore encoded for a secret stops matching *.jks/*.keystore and would
# otherwise slip past every rule above.
keystore.properties
signing.properties
upload-keystore.*
upload_certificate.pem
*.keystore.base64
*.jks.base64
# Service-account JSON for the Play Developer Publishing API, if it is ever used.
play-publisher*.json
google-play-service-account*.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ------------------------------------------------------ generated build output
# build/ is a committed directory (build/.gitkeep) but its contents are
# per-run artifacts: CI uploads them, git never stores them.
build/*
!build/.gitkeep

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- Python tools
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ------------------------------------------------- Substrate Kit local state
# HANDOFF.md is regenerated by the kit at every session boot and is untracked by
# design (it says so in its own header) — it is a pointer to the newest session
# card, not a record. The cards under .sessions/ are the durable memory.
/HANDOFF.md
